 ],
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "ru_01",
   "t": 1.85,
   "who": "narrator",
   "voice": "narrator",
   "maxSec": 14.6,
   "ref": "Ruth 1:1-5",
   "zh": "很久以前，有一位老妈妈，叫拿俄米。她的丈夫和两个儿子……都去世了。她的身边，只剩下儿媳妇路得。",
   "en": "Long ago, there was a woman named Naomi. Her husband and her two sons had died... and now only Ruth, her son's wife, was left with her.",
   "dir": "storyteller opening; soft and slow, a real pause before 都去世了 / 'had died'; tender, never gloomy",
   "dur": 14.55,
   "pre": 0.25,
   "post": 0.4,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "",
    "edge": "origin",
    "dt": 1.85
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_02",
   "t": 17.3,
   "who": "naomi",
   "voice": "naomi",
   "maxSec": 9.14,
   "ref": "Ruth 1:8-9",
   "zh": "路得啊……我要回伯利恒老家了。你还年轻，回你娘家去吧，啊？",
   "en": "Ruth, my dear... I'm going home to Bethlehem. You're still young. Go back to your mother's house, all right?",
   "dir": "tired, loving, a little choked; a sigh before she starts; the last 啊 / 'all right' is soft, almost begging",
   "dur": 9.09,
   "pre": 0.5,
   "post": 0.6,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_01",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 0.9
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_03",
   "t": 27.89,
   "who": "ruth",
   "voice": "ruth",
   "maxSec": 10.6,
   "ref": "Ruth 1:16",
   "zh": "不，我不走！你往哪里去，我也往哪里去；你住在哪里，我也住在哪里。你的上帝……就是我的上帝。",
   "en": "No, I won't leave you! Where you go, I will go. Where you stay, I will stay. Your God... will be my God.",
   "dir": "heartfelt, close to tears but steady; quick and firm on 不我不走, then slower and warmer; a breath before 你的上帝 / 'Your God'; the most important line in the story",
   "dur": 10.55,
   "pre": 0.9,
   "post": 0.6,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_02",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 1.5
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_04",
   "t": 40.74,
   "who": "narrator",
   "voice": "narrator",
   "maxSec": 9.52,
   "ref": "Ruth 1:19, 1:22",
   "zh": "她们走呀走，走了好远好远的路，终于回到了伯利恒。那时候，正是收大麦的季节。",
   "en": "They walked and walked, a long, long way, and at last they came to Bethlehem. It was barley harvest time.",
   "dir": "the walking rhythm in the voice (走呀走); brighter on 终于 / 'at last'; a small smile on the harvest",
   "dur": 9.47,
   "pre": 0.3,
   "post": 0.3,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_03",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 2.3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_05",
   "t": 51.11,
   "who": "naomi",
   "voice": "naomi",
   "maxSec": 8.26,
   "ref": "Ruth 1:21",
   "zh": "唉……我走的时候，什么都有。回来的时候……什么都没有了。",
   "en": "Oh... when I left, I had everything. Now I've come home... with nothing.",
   "dir": "a long sigh first; quiet, empty; slow, with a break before the second half",
   "dur": 8.21,
   "pre": 0.6,
   "post": 0.5,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_04",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 0.9
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_06",
   "t": 60.12,
   "who": "ruth",
   "voice": "ruth",
   "maxSec": 5.26,
   "ref": "Ruth 2:2",
   "zh": "婆婆，别难过。我去田里拾麦穗，咱们就有饭吃啦！",
   "en": "Don't be sad, Mother. I'll go and pick up grain in the fields, then we'll have food to eat!",
   "dir": "gentle first, then bright and eager, a little smile; quicker at the end",
   "dur": 5.21,
   "pre": 0.3,
   "post": 0.4,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_05",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 0.8
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_07",
   "t": 68.13,
   "who": "narrator",
   "voice": "narrator",
   "maxSec": 10.16,
   "ref": "Ruth 2:2-3; Leviticus 19:9-10",
   "zh": "在以色列，割麦子的人会故意留下一些麦穗，给穷人捡。路得就跪在田边，一根一根地拾。",
   "en": "In Israel, the harvesters left some grain behind for poor people to pick up. So Ruth knelt at the edge of the field and picked it up, one stalk at a time.",
   "dir": "calm and explaining, like a parent pointing at a picture; slow on 一根一根 / 'one stalk at a time'",
   "dur": 10.11,
   "pre": 2.0,
   "post": 0.4,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_06",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 2.8
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_08",
   "t": 79.24,
   "who": "narrator",
   "voice": "narrator",
   "maxSec": 7.02,
   "ref": "Ruth 2:1, 2:3",
   "zh": "这块田的主人，叫波阿斯。他是个又有钱、又善良的好人。",
   "en": "The field belonged to a man named Boaz. He was rich, and he was very kind.",
   "dir": "warm, a little admiring",
   "dur": 6.97,
   "pre": 0.6,
   "post": 0.2,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_07",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 1.0
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_09",
   "t": 86.71,
   "who": "boaz",
   "voice": "boaz",
   "maxSec": 3.75,
   "ref": "Ruth 2:4",
   "zh": "大家辛苦啦！愿上帝和你们同在！",
   "en": "Good morning, everyone! The Lord be with you!",
   "dir": "hearty and friendly, loud enough to carry across a field; a big smile",
   "dur": 3.7,
   "pre": 0.3,
   "post": 0.1,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_08",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 0.5
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_10",
   "t": 90.61,
   "who": "reapers",
   "voice": "reapers",
   "maxSec": 2.46,
   "ref": "Ruth 2:4",
   "zh": "也愿上帝赐福给你！",
   "en": "The Lord bless you too!",
   "dir": "three or four workers answering together from across the field, cheerful, slightly ragged, not in perfect unison",
   "dur": 2.41,
   "pre": 0.1,
   "post": 0.4,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_09",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 0.2
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_11",
   "t": 94.22,
   "who": "boaz",
   "voice": "boaz",
   "maxSec": 2.54,
   "ref": "Ruth 2:5",
   "zh": "咦？那个姑娘是谁呀？",
   "en": "Hm? Who's that young woman over there?",
   "dir": "he stops mid-step, curious and gentle; a thinking 咦 / 'hm' first",
   "dur": 2.49,
   "pre": 0.8,
   "post": 0.3,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_10",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 1.2
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_12",
   "t": 99.11,
   "who": "boaz",
   "voice": "boaz",
   "maxSec": 8.93,
   "ref": "Ruth 2:8-9",
   "zh": "姑娘，你就在我的田里拾吧，别去别处了。渴了，就去那边罐子里喝水。",
   "en": "Stay here and gather in my field. Don't go anywhere else. And when you're thirsty, go and drink from the water jars.",
   "dir": "kind, fatherly, unhurried; points toward the jars on 那边 / 'water jars'",
   "dur": 8.88,
   "pre": 1.8,
   "post": 0.4,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_11",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 2.4
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_13",
   "t": 108.99,
   "who": "ruth",
   "voice": "ruth",
   "maxSec": 4.89,
   "ref": "Ruth 2:10",
   "zh": "我是外地来的……您为什么对我这么好呢？",
   "en": "I'm a stranger here... why are you so kind to me?",
   "dir": "shy, amazed, almost a whisper; the question rises gently",
   "dur": 4.84,
   "pre": 0.6,
   "post": 0.4,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_12",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 1.0
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_14",
   "t": 114.53,
   "who": "boaz",
   "voice": "boaz",
   "maxSec": 6.47,
   "ref": "Ruth 2:11-12",
   "zh": "你对婆婆的好，我都听说了。愿上帝好好报答你！",
   "en": "I've heard all about how good you've been to Naomi. May God reward you for it!",
   "dir": "warm and moved; a smile in the voice; the blessing a little slower",
   "dur": 6.42,
   "pre": 0.3,
   "post": 0.5,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_13",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 0.7
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_15",
   "t": 123.35,
   "who": "boaz",
   "voice": "boaz",
   "maxSec": 7.28,
   "ref": "Ruth 2:15-16",
   "zh": "嘘——割麦子的时候，故意多掉一些……留给她捡！嘿嘿。",
   "en": "Psst... when you cut the barley, drop a little extra on purpose... for her to pick up! Heh heh.",
   "dir": "stage whisper, playful, a grin; slow and secretive, then a cheeky lift on 留给她捡 / 'for her'",
   "dur": 7.23,
   "pre": 1.4,
   "post": 0.2,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_14",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 2.4
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_16",
   "t": 132.98,
   "who": "narrator",
   "voice": "narrator",
   "maxSec": 4.15,
   "ref": "Ruth 2:17",
   "zh": "到了晚上，路得捡了满满一大捆大麦！",
   "en": "By evening, Ruth had gathered a great big bundle of barley!",
   "dir": "building delight; big and round on 满满一大捆 / 'great big bundle'",
   "dur": 4.1,
   "pre": 0.6,
   "post": 0.2,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_15",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 2.4
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_17",
   "t": 137.88,
   "who": "naomi",
   "voice": "naomi",
   "maxSec": 8.27,
   "ref": "Ruth 2:19",
   "zh": "哇！这么多呀！你今天……在谁的田里拾的？",
   "en": "Oh my! So much! Whose field were you working in today?",
   "dir": "genuinely amazed, the first time she sounds happy; laughs a little on 这么多呀 / 'so much'",
   "dur": 8.22,
   "pre": 0.6,
   "post": 0.3,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_16",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 0.8
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_18",
   "t": 146.6,
   "who": "ruth",
   "voice": "ruth",
   "maxSec": 3.03,
   "ref": "Ruth 2:19",
   "zh": "一个叫波阿斯的人。他对我可好啦！",
   "en": "A man called Boaz. He was so kind to me!",
   "dir": "happy, a bit breathless, proud",
   "dur": 2.98,
   "pre": 0.2,
   "post": 0.3,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_17",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 0.5
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_19",
   "t": 150.18,
   "who": "naomi",
   "voice": "naomi",
   "maxSec": 8.98,
   "ref": "Ruth 2:20",
   "zh": "波阿斯？他是我们的亲人哪！感谢上帝……他没有忘记我们！",
   "en": "Boaz? Why, he's family! Thank God... He hasn't forgotten us!",
   "dir": "surprise turning into joy and thankful tears; a catch in the voice before 他没有忘记我们",
   "dur": 8.93,
   "pre": 0.3,
   "post": 0.6,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_18",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 0.6
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_20",
   "t": 160.51,
   "who": "narrator",
   "voice": "narrator",
   "maxSec": 10.36,
   "ref": "Ruth 3:1-6",
   "zh": "拿俄米想：要是波阿斯能照顾路得，那该多好啊！一天晚上，路得去打谷场找波阿斯。",
   "en": "Naomi thought, 'If only Boaz would take care of Ruth!' So one night, Ruth went to find Boaz at the threshing floor.",
   "dir": "hushed, night-time, a little secret and hopeful",
   "dur": 10.31,
   "pre": 0.8,
   "post": 0.2,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_19",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 1.4
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_21",
   "t": 171.52,
   "who": "ruth",
   "voice": "ruth",
   "maxSec": 6.44,
   "ref": "Ruth 3:9",
   "zh": "波阿斯，您是我们的亲人……求您照顾我们一家，好吗？",
   "en": "Boaz, you're part of our family... will you please take care of us?",
   "dir": "soft, nervous, brave; small breath before 求您 / 'will you please'",
   "dur": 6.39,
   "pre": 0.5,
   "post": 0.5,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_20",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 0.7
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_22",
   "t": 178.71,
   "who": "boaz",
   "voice": "boaz",
   "maxSec": 7.15,
   "ref": "Ruth 3:10-11",
   "zh": "女儿，别怕。大家都知道，你是个好女子。我一定照顾你们！",
   "en": "Don't be afraid, my daughter. Everyone knows you're a good woman. I will take care of you, I promise!",
   "dir": "very gentle, then firm and sure on the promise; a smile",
   "dur": 7.1,
   "pre": 0.3,
   "post": 0.6,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_21",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 0.8
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_23",
   "t": 189.41,
   "who": "narrator",
   "voice": "narrator",
   "maxSec": 4.94,
   "ref": "Ruth 4:9-13",
   "zh": "后来，波阿斯娶了路得。全城的人都来祝福他们！",
   "en": "And so Boaz married Ruth. The whole town came to celebrate with them!",
   "dir": "bright and happy, a smile you can hear",
   "dur": 4.89,
   "pre": 2.4,
   "post": 0.6,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_22",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 3.6
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_24",
   "t": 195.9,
   "who": "narrator",
   "voice": "narrator",
   "maxSec": 5.52,
   "ref": "Ruth 4:13, 4:17",
   "zh": "不久，他们生了一个小宝宝，名字叫俄备得。",
   "en": "Before long, they had a baby boy. They named him Obed.",
   "dir": "soft and tender, like looking into a cradle; slow on the name",
   "dur": 5.47,
   "pre": 1.0,
   "post": 0.3,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_23",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 1.6
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_25",
   "t": 202.07,
   "who": "naomi",
   "voice": "naomi",
   "maxSec": 5.9,
   "ref": "Ruth 4:14-16",
   "zh": "我的小孙子……上帝真的没有忘记我！",
   "en": "My little grandson... God really didn't forget me!",
   "dir": "happy tears, half laughing; rocking rhythm; the last words full of wonder",
   "dur": 5.85,
   "pre": 0.4,
   "post": 0.6,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_24",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 0.7
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_26",
   "t": 209.12,
   "who": "narrator",
   "voice": "narrator",
   "maxSec": 8.38,
   "ref": "Ruth 4:17, 4:22",
   "zh": "你知道吗？俄备得长大以后，有个孙子叫大卫——就是打败歌利亚的那个大卫！",
   "en": "And guess what? When Obed grew up, he had a grandson named David. Yes, the David who beat Goliath!",
   "dir": "playful, leaning in to share a secret; a big happy reveal on 大卫 / 'David'",
   "dur": 8.33,
   "pre": 0.6,
   "post": 0.5,
   "anchor": {
    "line": "ru_25",
    "edge": "end",
    "dt": 1.2
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ru_27",
   "t": 218.55,
   "who": "narrator",
   "voice": "narrator",
   "maxSec": 7.35,
   "ref": "Ruth 1:16, 2:12",
   "zh": "路得对婆婆不离不弃，上帝也一直看顾着她们。你也可以好好爱你的家人哦！",
